# Cloudflare Pages redirects — pretty Spanish vanity paths -> the real /es/* pages.
# Keeps declareandbelieve.com/bienvenido (shown in Ayuda y soporte) working while
# the canonical pages stay under /es/.
/bienvenido /es/bienvenido 301
/ayuda /es/ayuda 301
/luchas /es/luchas 301
/dar /es/precios 301
/acerca /es/acerca 301
/privacidad /es/privacidad 301
/terminos /es/terminos 301

# ── Donation retirement (Release C1) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The giving product is removed. These are permanent, ONE HOP each — /es/dar
# goes straight to the Spanish page rather than via /pricing?lang=es, which
# would be a chain and would leak a query-string URL into the crawl graph.
# Query strings are not matched by Cloudflare Pages, so old links such as
# /give?status=success land on /pricing through the same rule. That is
# intentional: there is no public donor history to acknowledge.
/give        /pricing      301
/es/dar      /es/precios   301
# Historical giving terms. No public donation was ever taken, so no party
# relies on these; they are retired rather than rewritten as subscription
# terms, which would misrepresent a different transaction. Plus has its own
# terms on /plus.
/give-terms                  /pricing     301
/es/terminos-de-donacion     /es/precios  301
